messages:
jane.dev: Heads-up — hit runtime errors in Cloudflare Workers when the SDK calls crypto.createHash(Buffer). Error: 'crypto.createHash is not a function'. Anyone owning a short-term fallback plan?

sam.eng: Yep saw that in a customer repro. Workers has Web Crypto (crypto.subtle) but no Node 'crypto' module. Stack trace points at a third-party lib expecting a Hash object.

marta.devex: We prototyped a tiny shim that maps createHash(...).update(...).digest('hex') -> subtle.digest + hex encode. Typings are the annoying bit: @types/node expects methods on Hash and Buffer inputs.

sam.eng: Example shim we used (async digest wrapper):
```js
const { subtle } = globalThis.crypto;
function createHash(algo) {
  let chunks = [];
  return {
    update(chunk) { chunks.push(typeof chunk === 'string' ? new TextEncoder().encode(chunk) : chunk); return this },
    async digest(enc) {
      const bytes = chunks.length === 1 ? chunks[0] : new Uint8Array(chunks.flatMap(c => Array.from(c)));
      const res = await subtle.digest(algo === 'sha256' ? 'SHA-256' : algo, bytes);
      if (enc === 'hex') return Array.from(new Uint8Array(res)).map(b => b.toString(16).padStart(2,'0')).join('');
      return new Uint8Array(res);
    }
  }
}
module.exports = { createHash };
```

ryan.docs: Thanks for snippet — we should ship a documented module like 'edge-compat/crypto' and call it out in the Workers quickstart. Also add guidance for size tradeoffs.

luis.sre: Concern: adding polyfills can bloat bundles. Can we lazy-load them only when runtime detection fails? e.g. `const createHash = typeof crypto?.createHash === 'function' ? require('crypto').createHash : await import('./worker-createhash.js')` — but note dynamic import + CJS interop is messy across bundlers.

nate: Another edge: some runtimes differ on TextEncoder/TextDecoder availability. Add a tiny encode util that falls back to Buffer when present, otherwise TextEncoder.

marta.devex: Typing plan: expose function signatures that accept BufferLike | Uint8Array | string and return Promise<string|Uint8Array>. Provide separate ambient types for worker builds (declare module 'edge-compat/crypto' with createHash return type union). Also update tsconfig docs for consumers using `skipLibCheck` as a temporary workaround.

jane.dev: Proposed next steps: 1) short RFC + design doc with options (shim vs optional dep vs upstream lib patch), 2) example in examples/worker-crypto-shim, 3) docs page and a small test harness in wrangler. I'll open the issue and mark priority P1 for onboarding-critical flows.

sam.eng: I'll draft the RFC & a minimal PR with lazy runtime detection + worker shim. Will add perf numbers for common payload sizes.

buildbot: Deploy preview created for branch workers-crypto-shim: https://preview.deep/branches/workers-crypto-shim (tests: 18 passed, 2 flaky skipped) :white_check_mark:

ryan.docs: I'll reserve a docs slot and draft the 'Worker compatibility' subsection describing limitations and the shim approach.

luis.sre: Quick note — add an A/B policy to the runtime router so we can route some customers to the new shim path for evaluation without global rollout.

jane.dev: Great. Thanks all — assign follow-ups in the issue. :thumbsup:
